<div id="A13.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A13.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="790.34" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 790.34" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,790.34) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="0.5" stroke="#808080" stroke-opacity="0.5"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.54 -3.54 L 3.54 786.8 L 553.54 786.8 L 553.54 -3.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 790.34 L 550 790.34 L 550 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.11 1.11 L 1.11 789.23 L 548.89 789.23 L 548.89 1.11 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.88 18.88)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.02em;--ltx-fo-height:54.39em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="752.59" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 752.59)" width="512.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A13.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-sectional-block ltx_minipage">
                  
<section id="A13.SS0.SSSx10" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Medium Question with excess High-Entropy Tokens (Incorrect Answer)</h4>

<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">difficulty:</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Medium</span></span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Gen_high_entropy_token:</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 84</span></span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Threshold(medium):</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 55</span></span></span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Entropy reward:</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 0.38</span></span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">acc reward:</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 0.0</span></span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">overall reward:</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p1.1.2.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> 0.38</span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Okay, let’s try</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to figure out how to find </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The problem involves a diagram with a green square and a blue square connected. There is a point </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with a segment of length </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and another segment labeled </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Wait, maybe</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> the diagram is a cube net, since dashed lines often indicate hidden edges. If </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FW=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FW=10</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WW^{\prime}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WW^{\prime}=4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, perhaps </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the distance from </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Alternatively</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, maybe this is related to vectors or a triangle. If </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> form sides of a right triangle, then</span></span>
<span id="A13.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}=10^{2}+4^{2}=116,\quad x=\sqrt{116}=2\sqrt{29}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">116</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">116</mn></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">29</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}=10^{2}+4^{2}=116,\quad x=\sqrt{116}=2\sqrt{29}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">But hold on</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, maybe the 10 and 4 are not perpendicular. Then by the Law of Cosines:</span></span>
<span id="A13.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}=10^{2}+4^{2}-2\cdot 10\cdot 4\cos\theta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}=10^{2}+4^{2}-2\cdot 10\cdot 4\cos\theta,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">but without </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p5.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, this is indeterminate.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Next</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, let me try coordinates. Suppose </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(0,0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(0,0,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">If</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=(10,0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=(10,0,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}=(10,4,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}=(10,4,0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, then</span></span>
<span id="A13.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FW^{\prime}=\sqrt{10^{2}+4^{2}}=\sqrt{116}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">116</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FW^{\prime}=\sqrt{10^{2}+4^{2}}=\sqrt{116}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Alternatively</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, if </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}=(10,0,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}=(10,0,4)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the distance is also </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{116}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">116</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{116}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">…(several further “wait” moments about whether this is a parallelogram, trapezoid, or 3D projection are omitted here) …</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Another thought</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: perhaps FW and WW’ are adjacent edges of a cube net, so </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the straight-line distance from </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Therefore</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p9.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, again,</span></span>
<span id="A13.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sqrt{10^{2}+4^{2}}=2\sqrt{29}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">29</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sqrt{10^{2}+4^{2}}=2\sqrt{29}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Yet</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, could it be colinear? If so, </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=10+4=14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=10+4=14</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p10.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. But that seems inconsistent with the diagram.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Maybe</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> it’s a right triangle hidden in the net. If FW is one leg, WW’ another, then </span><math id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the hypotenuse.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Finally</span><span id="A13.SS0.SSSx10.p12.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, after multiple conflicting attempts, the reasoning converges to</span></span>
<span id="A13.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=2\sqrt{29}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">29</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=2\sqrt{29}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</section>
                </span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
